# Modular Monolith Rules

## Architecture

- Deliver as a modular monolith inside one Django project.
- Do not introduce microservices, separate deployable domain services, or event-bus-first designs without an approved ADR.

## Module boundaries

Each domain module owns its models and public service API.

Allowed patterns:

- `services.py` — business operations and writes
- `selectors.py` — complex reads and query composition
- `policies.py` — authorization and separation-of-duty checks
- `models.py` — persistence owned by the module

## Dependency rules

- Other modules must call public services/selectors, not reach into private model internals across boundaries when a public API exists.
- Views and templates must not embed domain business logic.
- Cross-module writes that touch multiple aggregates must run inside explicit database transactions.
- Avoid circular module dependencies; extract shared primitives carefully and sparingly.

## Future extraction

Modules may be extracted only when scale, team, or deployment needs justify the cost, and only after an approved ADR.
